{
  "name": "What Happens During Water Damage Repair?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When water damage hits, it can feel overwhelming, but a clear process makes all the difference. First, we've got to stop the source of the water – whether it's a leaky pipe or something else. Once that's handled, we'll get right to assessing all the damage, including what might be hidden behind walls or under floors. This is super important because water can seep into places you wouldn't expect. Next up is drying out the affected area thoroughly, which usually takes about 3 to 5 days, depending on how much water there was and how widespread the damage is. We use specialized equipment to make sure everything is completely dry to prevent future problems like mold. Finally, we'll tackle any secondary issues that pop up, like rotting wood, swelling drywall, or other structural concerns. It's a comprehensive approach to get your home back to normal. If you're in the Denver area and dealing with water damage, don't wait. Give us a call at 303-505-0866, and let's get things dried out and repaired properly.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
